{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
  "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lisa S. Blatt (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Schooner Exchange held that general laws describing admiralty jurisdiction do not reach foreign sovereigns. The reasons for that clear statement rule -- notice and equality among independent nations -- apply with greater force here. It is outlandish to think that Section 3231 authorizes federal courts to convict Spain."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lisa S. Blatt (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Schooner Exchange, after all, is an instrumentality case, a ship. And the FSIA defines foreign states to include instrumentalities. U.S. instrumentalities like the Export-Import Bank are sovereign."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Ms. Blatt, just so I can analytically -- could understand analytically your argument, could you waive immunity in -- in district court and would -- after the waiver, would they have jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see anything in this statute that suggests that Congress was focused on or was thinking about immunity for criminal prosecution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, again, what worries me and why I think Congress should have a vote is I don't think -- not every President and every foreign country may feel the way our President does."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But, if we disagree with you about the criminal grant of jurisdiction, does that argument work as well?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "anything at all about procedures or anything else when it came to criminal cases because there's no such thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: -- right now, have states even tried it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FEIGIN",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner is asking for an extraordinary and unprecedented rule under which any foreign government-owned corporation could become a clearinghouse for any federal crime, including interfering in our elections, stealing our nuclear secrets, or something like here, evading our sanctions and funneling billions of dollars to an embargoed nation, using our banks, and lying to our regulators."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FEIGIN",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ERIC J. FEIGIN ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: On the state -- state prosecution question that came up, my understanding was that if states tried to do a prosecution of something --in something like this, that the federal government could submit a statement of interest, and the foreign affairs preemption doctrine exists to ensure that that kind of activity doesn't occur and, if it did occur, that this Court would be available to review that kind of action by a state. Is that Garamendi, cases like that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- counsel, I'm wondering to what extent you've considered the impact, though, of -- of saying that 1604 doesn't provide immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Isn't your answer yes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if a --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- when Congress enacted the FSIA, Congress was changing the common law with respect to instrumentalities of sovereign states in that dramatic a fashion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, under what theory would this state prosecution be preempted by federal law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: A couple --couple follow-ups. You said earlier you were representing all the executive departments and agencies. You're representing the President too, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Your Honor, I'd prefer not to discuss the details of internal processes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edb0b8124f11f48b3d4428a9e9974b3750954292a138fe11785f0833c765d9a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edb0b8124f11-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:44 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
